    "body": "it turns out you can just emit SGR sequences yourself instead of asking an embedded virtual machine to do it for you.\r\n\r\nterminfo capabilities `set_attributes` and friends are almost identical when they are available. the only difference between terminals is what subset of features are available. but emitting unknown SGR sequences is considered to be safe, they are just ignored by the terminal. We already use this \"logic\" for altfont, so let's apply that to everything.\r\n\r\nThe main capability that _needs_ to be detected is the number of supported colors `num_colors`. This is what for the failing tests either need to be fixed or adjust the tests (sometimes the behaviour is inconsistent with the description?)\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n  Thank you for contributing to Neovim!\r\n  If this is your first time, check out https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#pull-requests-prs\r\n  for our PR guidelines.\r\n-->\r\n",
